+# Delivered source excerpt — *Völuspá* 19
+
+Work: *The Elder Eddas of Saemund Sigfusson & The Younger Eddas of Snorre Sturleson*, Benjamin Thorpe (Elder Eddas translation) and I. A. Blackwell (Younger Eddas translation), Rasmus B. Anderson, editor in chief, 1906 edition, Project Gutenberg eBook 14726: <https://www.gutenberg.org/files/14726/14726-h/14726-h.htm>.
+
+Passage-level locator: “THE ELDER EDDAS OF SAEMUND” → “VOLUSPA” → stanza 19 (the stanza number as printed in the translation).
+
+> 19. I know an ash standing\
+> Yggdrasil hight,
+> a lofty tree, laved with limpid water:\
+> thence come the dews into the dales that fall;\
+> ever stands it green over Urd's fountain.
+
+This excerpt is supplied to make the cited image-level comparison inspectable. It is not an in-world source.
